Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 21:57:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(pl18ev): map the 3-state stick buttons to rest 0 / up
 +100 / down -100

The buttons on top of the Paladin EV sticks (EXT3/EXT4) are 3-state
resistor buttons. Read as multipos switches they did not work; read as
pots they give +100 % at rest, 0 % pressed down and -100 % pressed up.

Configure them as centered pots by default and turn the calibrated value
into a centered 3-state value (rest 0, up +100 %, down -100 %), debounced
by 50 ms because the signal passes the "down" level on its way to "up".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JtPRHfcjthyC8ptCnBrhPD
---
 radio/src/boards/hw_defs/pl18ev.json |  4 +--
 radio/src/mixer.cpp                  | 50 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 52 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

